# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/next-1 windows (the ship-5 candidate; scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/next-1 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN, ONE TAG AT A TIME (wait for the run to finish; never cancel a running card job).
# Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from the branch by its author. ORDER.txt, ORDER-W2.txt and
# ORDER-SHIP.txt have the order, the stop rules, the minutes and the read rules of the three runs.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next-1 is a PLACEHOLDER for the tag B0 builds from the pushed branch head WITH the K64j-OQ graft (sed -i 's/tp4-next-1/<tag>/' *.env). A commit of a file
# the image carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. This window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
# C2_MODEL_REPO / C2_MODEL_REVISION (qwen_c2_checkpoint.py): a job that carries them serves the Swift checkpoint (what production serves) from its own converted-weight directory and, since NP9, with the output
# ceiling of its catalog entry; the keys are the same in every smoke job of this pack, so each pair differs by the profile alone. The prefix, replay and build steps do not forward the selection (the job reader
# refuses the keys beside them): they run the base checkpoint, which is what their question (exactness of reuse against a cold twin of the same boot; the platform sequence) does not depend on.
# A2 (EXACT RESUME against a COLD TWIN, the strict pair read agent_turns does not make: agent_turns proves reuse and measures it, A2 proves every hit equal to its cold
# prefill): c2_prefix_gate.py --plan exact-resume on the audited twin c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-s5-audit, no baseline: first prompts of about 9k, 33k
# and 120k tokens, then returning tool turns of 150, 400, 900, 1,700, 2,600 and 300 new tokens, EVERY turn a cold/hit pair under a fresh salt, on sticky sessions with the
# undrop and the drafter-window carry and their audits, beside the lone-user padded round (each request here is alone: every round is a lone-user padded round with every
# audit on), the preconverted checkpoints and the tier at its new size. It runs on the BASE checkpoint (the prefix step does not forward the selection; exactness is a cold
# twin of the same boot, which does not depend on the weights). READ: the plan verdict PASS, every pair IDENTICAL, the oracle's Q equal to the hit's Q on every turn,
# "window carry carried" lines on the turns that fit the window and "window carry audit ... exact=True" with the carried window's digest equal to the cold twin's, no "audit
# mismatch", no "fell back", no stall, no program compiled by a hit after its cold twin. SOFT: a failure here is NO-GO for the exact-resume lines of the candidate
# (QWEN_PREFIX_STICKY_UNDROP and QWEN_PREFIX_WINDOW_CARRY in the ship entry of scripts/ci/fusion-wp/S5.json), not for the rest; read it before the owner approves. Estimate
# 55 minutes (the ER pack's ERX estimated 50). RUN WITH THE CI PAUSED: the ARC runner sets are at ZERO for this job (ORDER, ARC-ZERO); no build, no CI push, no other job
# beside it.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset prefix
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next-1
C2_PREFIX_PLAN=exact-resume
C2_PREFIX_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-s5-audit
C2_PREFIX_BASELINE=none
C2_BOX_MINUTES=120
